## Klondike Solitaire Card Game
-- See [wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Klondike_(solitaire)) for rules & naming conventions.
// What's where, top to bottom:  each part uses only what's above it
//   the solitaire:  what it has, how it lays out its table, and its moves
//   playing a card:  what a click does
//   what the solitaire does, once it can play a card:  auto-play, reset, cheat, drawing
//   start
//   the piles:  each kind, what it may take or give up, and how it draws


## The solitaire:  what it has
a solitaire is an app where:
	- its score is a number
	- its stock is a stock pile
	- its discards is a discard pile
	- its foundations is a list of foundations
	- its tableaus is a list of tableaus
	- its deck is a deck

	// one of each pile, then every card in the stock
	- to lay out a solitaire:
		set its stock to a new stock pile with name = "stock", droppable = no
		set its discards to a new discard pile with name = "discards", droppable = no

		set clubs-pile to a new foundation with name = clubs, symbol = "♣️", droppable = yes
		add clubs-pile to its foundations
		set diamonds-pile to a new foundation with name = diamonds, symbol = "♦️", droppable = yes
		add diamonds-pile to its foundations
		set hearts-pile to a new foundation with name = hearts, symbol = "♥️", droppable = yes
		add hearts-pile to its foundations
		set spades-pile to a new foundation with name = spades, symbol = "♠️", droppable = yes
		add spades-pile to its foundations

		for each number from 1 to 7
			set column to a new tableau with name = ("T" + the number), droppable = yes
			add column to its tableaus

		set its deck to a new deck
		set up its deck
		for each card in its deck
			add the card to the stock of the solitaire

	- its state is:
		set state to a new list of text
		for each pile in every pile
			add the state of the pile to state
		return state

	- to debug a solitaire:
		for each line of its state
			print the line

	- to reset the stock of a solitaire:
		set cards to a copy of list (its discards) as a pile
		reverse the cards
		for each card in the cards
			add it to the stock of the solitaire
			turn the card face down

	- animation play from the stock of a solitaire:
		if its stock is empty
			wait for: reset the stock of it

		get the bottom card of its stock
		turn it face up
		// pause for 150 msec
		move it to the discards of the solitaire

	- animation deal the cards of a solitaire:
		// pull all cards into stock with a nice animation
		set cards to merge every pile into a new pile
		reverse the cards
		for each card in the cards
			set start-pile to the pile of the card
			turn the card face down
			if start-pile is not the stock of the solitaire
				add the card to the stock of the solitaire
				pause for 50 msec
		shuffle its stock

		// deal cards into tableaus
		for row from 1 to 7
			turn the bottom card of its stock face up
			for column from row to 7
				add the bottom card of its stock to item column of its tableaus
				pause for 50 msec

		wait for: play from the stock of it

set the solitaire to a new solitaire
lay out the solitaire
print the solitaire


## Playing a card:  what a click does
to play a card
	set start-pile to the pile of the card
	if start-pile cannot give up the card return no

	if start-pile is the stock of the solitaire
		play from the stock of the solitaire
		return

	set end-pile to the first pile in piles in every pile where its droppable is yes and it can take the card
	if there is not an end-pile return no

	set cards-to-move to cards in start-pile starting with the card
	set the name of cards-to-move to the name of the start-pile
	print "moving (" + the state of cards-to-move + ") to (" + the state of end-pile + ")"

	for each card in cards-to-move
		move it to end-pile

	if the start-pile is a tableau and the start-pile is not empty
		pause for 200 msec
		get the last card of the start-pile
		print "turning over (" + the name of start-pile + ": " + its state + ")"
		turn it face up

	if end-pile is a foundation: set the score of the solitaire to the score of the solitaire + 10
	else if start-pile is the discards of the solitaire: set the score of the solitaire to the score of the solitaire + 5
	return yes

on card-click with a card
	play the card


## What the solitaire does, once it can play a card
a solitaire:
	- to auto-play a solitaire:
		set anything-changed to no
		if its discards is not empty
			set test-card to the last card of its discards
			if await play test-card
				set anything-changed to yes
				pause for 500 msec

		// attempt to move bottom card of tableaus to foundations
		for each pile in its tableaus
			if the pile is empty return
			set test-card to the last card in the pile
			set foundation to the first pile in piles in the foundations of the solitaire where the name of the pile is the suit of test-card
			if the foundation can take test-card
				set anything-changed to yes
				await play test-card
				pause for 100 msec

		// attempt to move the entire pile of face-up cards
		for each pile in its tableaus
			set face-up-cards to the cards in the pile where the card is face up
			if face-up-cards is empty return
			set test-card to the first card in face-up-cards
			if test-card is a king and test-card is the first card of the pile return
			if await play test-card
				set anything-changed to yes
				pause for 500 msec

		// call auto-play again if anything actually changed
		if anything-changed await auto-play it

	- to reset a solitaire:
		set its score to 0
		deal the cards of it

	- to cheat at a solitaire:
		set remaining-piles to piles in its tableaus where it is not empty and its first card is face down
		if remaining-piles is empty return
		set the pile to a random pile in remaining-piles
		set unplaid-cards to cards in the pile where the card is face down
		set card to a random card in unplaid-cards
		turn the card face up
		pause for 30 ticks
		move the card to the discards of the solitaire

	- to draw a solitaire:
		return <div className="ui container">
			<div className="board">
				<table className="ui table fixed">
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th colSpan="2" className="left aligned">Klondike Solitaire</th>
							<th className="right aligned">{"Score: " + its score}</th>
							<th><div className="tiny fluid ui button compact" onClick={auto-play it}>AutoPlay</div></th>
							<th><div className="tiny fluid ui button compact" onClick={cheat at it}>Cheat</div></th>
							<th><div className="tiny fluid ui button compact" onClick={debug it}>Debug</div></th>
							<th><div className="tiny fluid ui button compact" onClick={reset it}>Restart</div></th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
					<tr>
							<td>{draw its stock}</td>
							<td>{draw its discards}</td>
							<td></td>
							<td>{draw the first pile in its foundations}</td>
							<td>{draw the second pile in its foundations}</td>
							<td>{draw the third pile in its foundations}</td>
							<td>{draw the fourth pile in its foundations}</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
							<td>{draw item 1 of its tableaus}</td>
							<td>{draw item 2 of its tableaus}</td>
							<td>{draw item 3 of its tableaus}</td>
							<td>{draw item 4 of its tableaus}</td>
							<td>{draw item 5 of its tableaus}</td>
							<td>{draw item 6 of its tableaus}</td>
							<td>{draw item 7 of its tableaus}</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
		</div>


## Start
reset the solitaire
start the solitaire


## The piles:  each kind, what it may take or give up, and how it draws

// the stock:  cards not played yet
a stock pile is a pile
	- can give up a card if: the card is its bottom card
	- to draw a stock pile:
		return <div className="Pile Stock stacked">
			<div className="Placeholder ui button basic compact fluid" onClick={play from the stock of the solitaire}/>
			{draw its bottom card}
		</div>

// the discards:  where cards go as the stock is turned over
a discard pile is a pile
	- can give up a card if: the card is its bottom card
	- to draw a discard pile:
		return <div className="Pile Discards stacked">
			{draw its bottom card}
		</div>

// a foundation:  where a suit is built up, ace to king
a foundation is a pile
	- its symbol is text
	- can never let go of a card
	// one card at a time:  the last of its pile
	- can take a card if:
		if the card is not the bottom card of the pile of the card return no
		return its name is the suit of the card and its value + 1 is the value of the card
	- to draw a foundation:
		set color to "red" if its name is diamonds or its name is hearts otherwise "black"
		return <div className="Pile Foundation stacked">
			<div className={"Placeholder ui button basic compact fluid " + color + " " + its name}>
				<div className={"suit " + its name}>{its symbol}</div>
			</div>
			{draw its bottom card}
		</div>

// a tableau:  a column, built down from king to ace, red and black in turn
a tableau is a pile
	- can give up a card if: the card is face up
	- can take a card if:
		if the tableau is empty
			return the card is a king
		return its color is not the color of the card and its value is the value of the card + 1
	- to draw a tableau:
		return <div className="Pile Tableau staggered">
			{draw cards in it}
		</div>
